1.04

  Summary: Script layer rewritten as an additive patch. xAGNA adds to the animation tables at load and coexists with other NPC animation mods,
    and it restores every vanilla pose the old scripts dropped while keeping the new animations.

  Compatibility
    - The three full-file animation-table overrides give way to 2 additive scripts that patch the tables at load. xAGNA stops shipping those files, so it coexists with other NPC animation mods.

  Animations restored
    - Sentry, listening and searching NPCs play their poses on every weapon slot again. The old scripts had dropped several slots to a plain idle.
    - NPCs searching for a bloodsucker play the alert pose again. The old scripts left it blank.
    - The unarmed idle cycles its 4 variants again, and the duplicated idle entry is fixed.
    - Heavy-wounded variant 3 keeps its own distinct pose again.
    - Standing smoke plays the smoking animation again.

  Animations kept
    - The free-hand punch, the PDA draw on the idle, commander, guard and talk poses, the standing medical and wounded postures, and the re-animated motion set stay unchanged.

  Install
    - Delete the previous xAGNA, then install this version. It drops the old script files. Leaving them in place re-applies the old behavior.
